              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "DisplayContactsForJob"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1768294362127",
          "id": "1767963244907",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767963244910_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input: {{$context.$nodes.GETCONTACTSINFO.$output.result}} \n\nThe above input contains details about hiring team information for a job.\nFor each record in the above json, generate a cardWidget to display the details about the hiring team. Use the following details\ntitle must be a text saying \"Know Your Hiring Team\".\nUse \"patternId\": \"cardWidget\"\nproperties mapping:\nsubject: ContactName (concise, title case; 2–6 words if possible).\nsummary: A single 1–2 sentence string combining ContactEmail, and PhoneNumber in this format: \"Email • Phone\". If any of the field is null or empty, exclude that field.\ntimestamp: ContactPosition if present. Else exclude this field.\n\n**Display Logic for badgeText:**\n\n- If `ContactType` is present:\n  - If `ContactType` == \"HIRING_MANAGER\", show \"Hiring Manager\" in title case.\n  - Else if `ContactType` == \"RECRUITER\", show \"Recruiter\".\n\n\nvariant: \"info\"\n\nUse human-readable values; do not fabricate any data.\n\n\nEnsure each display uses a unique key and do not show any thinking or ask follow up questions."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CARD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "DisplayContactsForGig"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAYCONTACTSFORGIG",
          "id": "1768294392886",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768294392887_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input: {{$context.$nodes.GETCONTACTSINFO.$output.result}} \n\nThe above input contains details about team information for a gig.\nFor each record in the above json, generate a cardWidget to display the details about the hiring team. Use the following details\ntitle must be a text saying \"Know your hiring team\".\nUse \"patternId\": \"cardWidget\"\nproperties mapping:\nsubject: TeamMemberName(concise, title case; 2–6 words if possible).\nsummary: A single 1–2 sentence string combining TeamMemberEmailAddress. If GigManager is true, then display TeamMemberPhoneNumber(if value is not empty or not null) also in the format \"Email • Phone\"\ntimestamp: If Position field is not null or empty, display value of Position field. Else display TeamMemberRole\n\n**Display Logic for badgeText:**\n\n- If `GigManager` is true:\n  - show \"Gig Manager\" in title case.\n  - Else show \"Gig Team\" in title case.\n\n\nvariant: \"info\"\n\nUse human-readable values; do not fabricate any data.\n\n\nEnsure each display uses a unique key and do not show any thinking or ask follow up questions."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check For Empty Data"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1770060354805",
            "false": "add_false_1770060287963"
          },
